      "hints": [
        "Ratio $\\frac{S_{100}}{S_\\infty} = 1 - r^{100} = 1 - 0.99^{100}$.",
        "Calculate $1 - 0.99^{100} \\approx 0.634$.",
        "Percentage is $63\\%$ (2 s.f.)."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Write the formulae for $S_{100}$ and $S_\\infty$ and form their ratio:\n$$S_{100} = \\frac{a(1 - r^{100})}{1 - r}, \\quad S_\\infty = \\frac{a}{1 - r}$$\n$$\\frac{S_{100}}{S_\\infty} = \\frac{\\frac{a(1 - r^{100})}{1 - r}}{\\frac{a}{1 - r}} = 1 - r^{100}$$",
        "Substitute $r = 0.99$ into the ratio:\n$$\\frac{S_{100}}{S_\\infty} = 1 - 0.99^{100} \\approx 1 - 0.366032 = 0.633968$$",
        "Convert the ratio to a percentage (to 2 significant figures):\n$$\\text{Percentage} = 0.633968 \\times 100\\% \\approx 63.4\\% \\approx 63\\%$$"
      ],
